+++ b/boards/arm/nrf51_pca10028/nrf51_pca10028_defconfig
@@ -16,3 +16,6 @@ CONFIG_UART_0_NRF_UART=y
 # enable console
 CONFIG_CONSOLE=y
 CONFIG_UART_CONSOLE=y
+
+CONFIG_CLOCK_CONTROL_NRF_K32SRC_RC=y
+CONFIG_CLOCK_CONTROL_NRF_K32SRC_250PPM=y
```

review_comments:
Sorry for the delay. I've reproduced the problem. The proposed solution stops calibration because state machine stuck in that state as there is no asynchronous event to push it forward. I still think that simplest and most reasonable is to set unrealistic temperature. That will force calibration.

Something like:
```
if (rc != 0) {
  temperature = INT16_MAX;
  LOG_WRN("Temperature sensor not ready. Setting max temperature to enforce calibration.");
}
```

Initially, i thought about requesting temperature measurement again (`k_work_submit(&temp_measure_work)`) but that won't work as this work submit has higher priority so calling it recursively leads to deadlock.
